  "id": "prior-entry",
  "term": "prior entry",
  "definition": "Prior entry is the idea that attention makes an attended stimulus reach perceptual processing, including awareness, sooner than an unattended stimulus. It has been used to explain why two nearly simultaneous events may be experienced in the wrong temporal order.",
